<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for March 14.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for March 14.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Thursday released the following forecasts and data for gas consumption in the period March 12-14.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 12 (actual) 235 mcm, 55 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 13 (forecast) 239 mcm, 56 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 14 (forecast) 238 mcm, 56 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 12 (actual) 9.8 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.1 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 13 (forecast) 9.8 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.2 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 14 (forecast) 9.7 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.3 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption to supply on Thursday, with none expected on Friday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5387</p>
</text>
